parts=['<h1>PM8 — Seven-study dietary evidence recovery</h1><p>26 October 2026 · <strong>PASS WITH LIMITATIONS</strong> · Local, uncommitted implementation.</p><h2>What changed</h2><p>The earlier PM8 had one dietary weight-loss SOP and no admitted §3.1.1 input. The recovery adds a bounded DHA Type B/Direct relationship and a milled-flaxseed SOP. The mission, prior seven Findings, two Principles, existing admissions, KC relationships and SEC history are preserved.</p><ul><li><strong>DHA:</strong> circulating adiponectin modulation in defined oral formulations. The separate DHA-versus-EPA trial supports substance attribution; mixed fish oil and enriched canola alone do not. No secretion, receptor, ordinary-food efficacy or universal hormone-benefit claim.</li><li><strong>Flaxseed:</strong> studied whole milled-food protocol, not an ALA/lignan/fibre admission. Concurrent weight changes, attrition and later pooled uncertainty retained.</li><li><strong>Local glucocorticoids:</strong> Stomby qualifies the existing programme through adipose transcript evidence; Stimson retains the explicit local activity/expression null despite systemic changes.</li><li><strong>Soluble fibre:</strong> pooled null/heterogeneous results do not justify a generic endocrine claim.</li><li><strong>NADPH:</strong> unstructured §3.1.2 entry removed. The reaction explanation remains in SP1 within Evidence & Audit. No substitute substance, food edge or nutrient requirement was manufactured.</li></ul><h2>Discovery and scope correction</h2><p>Stomby and Stimson were already separately appraised. The other five mandatory papers had no separate appraisal record located; Gammelmark appeared in the already retrieved Wu review. This establishes a source-appraisal recovery gap, not proof that no agent ever saw the citation.</p><p>The previous blanket missing-delivery rationale was too broad: Gammelmark measured oral mixture delivery and adipose incorporation. Neither proves secretion. The current DHA admission concerns the circulating endocrine signal itself, not a proxy used to claim an unmeasured secretory or receptor mechanism. Clinical or ADHD benefit is not required or inferred.</p><h2>Evidence-access limitations</h2><p>Original flaxseed Methods, results and tables were inspected through the institutional full PDF. Rausch’s full author manuscript and the two 2023 review XMLs were recovered. Original primary full methods and supplements were not recovered for every target. The matrix distinguishes these limits; no full-paper review or complete risk-of-bias appraisal is claimed where unavailable. Pauls 2021 was held out after a correction notice was identified and its content could not be recovered.</p><h2>Study-by-study adjudication</h2>']
